# timers2: harder calendar expressions, several OnCalendar= lines
#
# A timer may have several OnCalendar= lines; it fires whenever any of them
# matches. Some things that are awkward in cron are easy here:
#   Mon *-*-01..07 03:00    a Monday that falls on day 1-7: the first Monday
#   *-*~01 23:00            "~" counts from the end of the month: last day
#   *-*~07/1 ...            the last 7 days of the month
# Watch out: the weekday and the date must BOTH match. "Mon *-*-01" means
# "the 1st, when it is a Monday", which happens only a few times a year.
#
# Task: maintenance should run at 03:00 on the first Monday of every month,
# and at 23:00 on the last day of every month (whatever its length). Fix the
# two lines below. Test them with `systemd-analyze calendar --iterations=6`.

[Unit]
Description=systemdlings: monthly maintenance windows

[Timer]
OnCalendar=Mon *-*-01 03:00
OnCalendar=*-*-31 23:00
